# DarkTask

Windows-first managed remote-control platform. Do not reuse IDs, tokens, or assumptions from other workspaces.

## Stack (this project)

- GitHub: `Blackh8t/DarkTask`
- Linux Rust server (`apps/server`) on the VPS behind Caddy (`rust.privateserver.im`)
- Windows agent (`apps/agent`) + controller (`apps/controller`)
- Android APK upload/download from the admin portal; install + enroll QR codes
- Flutter technician app scaffold: `apps/mobile_controller` (not the Android endpoint)

Not using Vercel or Supabase in this repo.

## Protocol

- Enroll `POST /api/v1/enroll`
- Agent WS `/ws/agent`
- Session WS `/ws/session/{id}?role=agent|controller&token=`
- Frames: RPF1 JPEG (Windows) or H.264 (Android, no audio, 1 Mbps / 12 fps / 1280px)

## Android endpoint constraints

scrcpy-server cannot run in a normal APK (needs ADB/shell). Capture is MediaProjection; input is AccessibilityService. No audio.
